            <ArticleTitle>Matricial Wasserstein-1 Distance.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>14-19</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1109/LCSYS.2017.2699319</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We propose an extension of the Wasserstein 1-metric (W1) for density matrices, matrix-valued density measures, and an unbalanced interpretation of mass transport. We use duality theory and, in particular, a &quot;dual of the dual&quot; formulation of W1. This matrix analogue of the Earth Mover's Distance has several attractive features including ease of computation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
